        ("p", "`break` leaves the nearest loop or switch immediately. `continue` skips the rest of this repetition and goes to the next test. `goto` jumps to a label. It is in the curriculum so you can recognise it. Do not use it in ordinary programs: a loop or a function states the intention more clearly, and a goto makes a long program hard to follow."),
